From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] rs6000: an integer TOC entry fits a TOC slot, not Pmode (cell64lv2)

The cell64lv2 ASM_OUTPUT_SPECIAL_POOL_ENTRY_P admitted an integer constant
into the TOC when its mode fit Pmode.  It was written when Pmode was SImode
under ILP32; since 0059 Pmode is DImode there, so with -mminimal-toc or
-mcmodel=small a DImode constant (unsigned long long f(void) { return
0x123456789abcdef0ULL; }) became a TOC entry.  An ILP32 TOC slot is
ptr_mode, 4 bytes, and output_toc asserts the constant fits it: -O0 died
with an internal compiler error.

Compare against ptr_mode, the slot's width.  ILP32 then keeps a DImode
constant out of the TOC and builds it inline as before 0059; LP64, where
ptr_mode is Pmode, is unchanged.

---
--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/cell64lv2.h
@@ -485,7 +485,7 @@
        || GET_CODE (X) == LABEL_REF					\
        || (CONST_INT_P (X)						\
 	   && TARGET_CMODEL != CMODEL_MEDIUM				\
-	   && GET_MODE_BITSIZE (MODE) <= GET_MODE_BITSIZE (Pmode))	\
+	   && GET_MODE_BITSIZE (MODE) <= GET_MODE_BITSIZE (ptr_mode)) \
        || (CONST_DOUBLE_P (X)						\
 	   && ((TARGET_64BIT						\
 		&& (TARGET_MINIMAL_TOC					\
